    "result_text": "All 38 tests pass with a clean build.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `contactPreference` derived field on the owner response so that it returns `EMAIL` when an email is present and `PHONE` otherwise.\n\nThe change follows the existing pattern for derived fields (like `membershipLevel`, `locality`, `bulkSignupWarning`), which are declared in the OpenAPI schema and computed in the MapStruct mapper:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property to the `Owner` schema, alongside the other derived fields.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` for `contactPreference` on `toOwnerDto`, backed by a `contactPreference(Owner)` helper that returns `\"EMAIL\"` for a non-blank email, else `\"PHONE\"` \u2014 mirroring the same email-presence check `membershipLevel` already uses.\n\nResults:\n- Both new `Cp27Tests` cases pass (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`).\n- Full suite: **38 tests run, 0 failures, 0 errors \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.**",
